# The command line and a file (#534). A fixture is run with nothing on its
# command line, so this sees no arguments and reads a file that is not
# there, which takes the `or`. A test of its own runs a program with
# arguments and a file to read.
arguments = System.arguments
puts arguments.length
p(arguments)
missing = System.read_file("/nonexistent/portland/file") || "nothing there"
puts missing
